 "honest": [
  "the warm slice pays the burn-in on bars before the measured span, so it prices the spec; the cold window is the same spec started at the era's own first bar, and the gap is the gate plus whatever the dead block accrued at the repo rate",
  "the pre2017 era starts where the panel starts, so its warm and cold quotes are the same curve by construction -- that is a disclosure, not a measurement",
  "the dead block is identified by the first decision the 250-bar rule allows, not by inspecting weights; no rebalance before it can hold a name",
  "the ratio of two rebased ann% is not a tradable sleeve, and era slices are not additive across eras",
  "descriptive census only: no gate, no verdict, no prereg, no trial count"
